# Line endings, explicit rather than left to core.autocrlf.
#
# This repository was authored on Windows with autocrlf=true, where every checkout rewrote every file and the
# diff for a one-line change became the whole file — worst of all in the Chinese documents, which are the bulk
# of the prose here. Storing LF and checking out LF makes the diff describe the change again.
* text=auto eol=lf

# `src/ui/desktop.ps1` starts with a UTF-8 BOM on purpose (see the README): Windows PowerShell 5.1 reads a
# BOM-less script in the system ANSI code page, which mangles the Chinese strings inside. `eol=lf` keeps the
# BOM at the top of the file where it belongs; nothing here may rewrite it.
*.ps1  text eol=lf

# Images and archives, should they ever be force-added. They are gitignored; this is the second line of
# defence, so a binary can never be text-mangled by a checkout.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.zip  binary
